1. Base Editor
VS Code — free, extensible, universal

The editor does not understand Python; the language server does.
Each edit ships a didChange notification across the wire, the server re-checks the file, and diagnostics come back to be drawn as squiggles and hovers.
Install the Python and Pylance extensions and this loop runs on every keystroke; skip them and the editor is a text box.

Now lets build it:

